{"availability":"available","full":"deepakcode21/Sorting-Algorithm-Visualizer","name":"Sorting-Algorithm-Visualizer","description":"A sorting algorithm visualizer makes learning fun by showing numbers sort themselves through colorful, animated steps.","category":"Design","language":"JavaScript","stars":17,"forks":3,"created":"2024-08-11T13:41:37Z","updated":"2025-01-02T16:18:23Z","branch":"main","homepage":"https://sortxtools.netlify.app/","topics":["bootstrap","css","html","javascript"],"demo":"https://sortxtools.netlify.app/","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T00:25:46.455Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-11T00:25:46.455Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-11T00:25:46.455Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-11T00:25:46.455Z","stars":17,"forks":3}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A sorting algorithm visualizer is like a colorful playground for numbers. You can watch as the numbers race, swap, and line up in perfect order, all with just a few clicks. It’s simple to use and fun to watch, turning complex code into an easy-to-follow animation. Whether it’s a slow bubble sort or a fast quicksort, each algorithm has its own unique style, making the whole process both entertaining and educational. Just sit back, relax, and enjoy the show as the numbers sort themselves out in a visually appealing way!"],"features":["Graphical User Interface (GUI) : The project comes with a user-friendly GUI that enables users to interact with the sorting algorithms visually.","Sorting Algorithms : The visualizer supports a variety of sorting algorithms, including but not limited to:","Real-Time Visualization : Users can observe the sorting algorithms in real-time, as the visualizer animates the sorting process step by step.","Adjustable Speed & Array size : The visualizer allows users to control the speed of the sorting animation, enabling them to slow down or speed up the visualization as per their preference."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.co